\par\pard\plain \sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John found himself intrigued, wandering alone through the halls he could not help but feel a childish sense of curiosity nibbling bite by bite at his focus. So much equipment scattered the rooms and desks that had all been but abandoned. There was an eerie, lonely yet exciting aura within each room. \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93342A, B, C, 343 \u8230\'85 343H!\u8221\'94 John counted in his thoughts,  scanning overhead the lab openings as he paced deeper into the facility, deeper into the mountain. Lab 343H had it\u8217\'92s blast doors sealed. \u8220\'93What secrets are you hiding that the Commander wants kept\u8221\'94 John thought to himself. he stood firmly against the door. He locked his mag boots to the steel grate below him. The terminal on the door had been fried, destroyed. \u8220\'93went to a bit of effort on this one. Hmph\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John began cutting a hole at the centre of the door his suit\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s  built in cutting torch extruded from the suit's wrist brace. Intended for ship repairs the tooling of the suit was useful in many scenario\u8217\'92s even breaching. A minute passed, John had cut out a hole large enough for his suits gauntlets to fit in and pry the doors open. He first inserted an Echo drone to check the close was clear. The scan revealed nothing but the usual scattered relics of the past computer systems, server stacks, although this room felt different. The equipment was larger, with a network of thick cabling was strewn across the lab floors like a tree's root system had been left to run wild. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John let out a prolonged strained grunt as the combined strength of him and his suit pried the door open. He stepped through and immediately the }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 gliding his finger tips over the countless unfamiliar relics from what seemed like a different age, but current to the day in their robustness. Instruments of science and engineering, Scattered in random, hinting at the life which once walked the halls. John found himself pulled into the remains of the abandoned facility eager to locate something missing. something seemed to be calling to him. This unexpected curiosity went against all his training, off guard. Johns trained state of caution and professionalism had been calmed by beauty. Elegantly designed human like machine arms clad plated with soft yet hardened alloys, humanly skin like feel to touch and look, met with course and exposed bearing linkages shoulder mounts grounded the witness to the mechanical nature. Amidst the scattered remnants of the room A dimly lit terminal posed itself to johns eye. It\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s green light dancing off the alloys scattered through the room.  Several options poised Johns curiosity across the terminal. John knew the potential consequences, insubordination, court marshal, dishonourable discharge. All the outcomes rushed through his mind fighting against the undying curiosity that something just did not seem right. For decades fear was bestowed upon them through what now seemed like propaganda. It was told that the facility had been overthrown in a hostile takeover, yet no signs of resistance or violence were present. The facility was abandoned and it seemed to have also been the nature of what had occurred. No weapons fire, disposed munitions, no bodies. Just remnants of marvels of design left to wither incomplete. If this was the case why were kill orders placed on confirmed sightings. What was the need to attain the data drives if their was no sign or evidence of resistance. Would the alliance not have copies already secured of everything they  needed? What minimal information led him and his men to believe a salvage operation. }
\par\pard\plain \li720\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 PRESS RESPECTIVE KEY FOR FOLLOWING:}
\par\pard\plain \li1080\fi-360\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \ls1\ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 1.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 HMNI Test Results.}
\par\plain \ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 2.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 Initiate HMNI Mobility Interface.}
\par\plain \ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 3.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 Initiate HMNI Neural Interface. }
\par\plain \ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 4.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 Initiate Full HMNI Interface. }
\par\pard\plain \li1080\fi-360\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \ls1\ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 5.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 New Entry. }
