\par\pard\plain \li1080\fi-360\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \ls2\ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 1.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 HMNITN1.}
\par\plain \ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 2.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 HMNIWT1.}
\par\pard\plain \li1080\fi-360\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \ls2\ilvl0{\listtext	\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 3.	}{\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 HMNIWT2. }
\par\pard\plain \li720\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 Project Fore Word, Doctor G.Wolfgang}
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 The ability to interface with the ether of not only electric energy spectrum seamlessly, A spectrum that lives in the body riding the flow through the blood like an invisible seamless network shaped like mycelium formed by strong currents. Becoming hyper focused the patient could tap in and accelerate their blood, generating energy to the frontal lobe simultaneously powering the communications module.   \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'931\u8221\'94 again. }
\par\pard\plain \sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 \tab HMNITN1 Human Machine Neural Interface Test Notes 1: }
\par\pard\plain \li720\sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 After becoming integrated following the HMNI Neural Integration with the facility I feel as though my nerves extend miles of cold yet spiking wire and steel, every actuation I feel like a tingling sensation in my body, an extension of my own synapses. Every flickering light, closing door, rewritten data block. I am plugged in, one with the facility. Systems running at 98% due to the set-backs ordered by the overhaul to rewrite interfaces for weapon trajectory control by commander illus. Interface control synapse reaction time has been measured highly responsive at 1 micro-Second, not considering the hardware response delays. Test commands are currently limited and continued to test operations. The interface upon closing my eyes feels like flying across a grid. Controlled by my mental visions\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92 direction. I can target highlighted nodes which represent and actuators, thanks to the ideation of our brilliant minds here at the facility. The control interface feels almost seamless and intuitive. All in all the test has been a complete but concerning test. Commander Illus seems to be ever determined to twist the program to his own \u8220\'93Scientific Will\u8221\'94 as he explains it. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8220\'93There are larger threats at play here that we all can\u8217\'92t consider without the United World Facilities, you would be swift to understand this Doctor! There are those in the system that won\u8217\'92t understand the project\u8221\'94 }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 My interpretation of the Commander is that he will stop at nothing to deliver utmost solar and galactic rule through the system by harnessing the sentient technology. }
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf4 \loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8230\'85This concludes Test1. }
\par\pard\plain \sa160\sl259\slmult1\ql\ltrch\loch \f0\fs24\b0\i0\cf5
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 Hitting Escape. John struggled to grasp what he was reading. He knew little of computer science, his training focused predominantly on survival, combat and rules of engagement to promote minimal loss of life, on both sides. However, this scientist wrote in simple terms giving clarity to what seemed a harmless interface between human and machine. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John lingered around the room captivated and overwhelmed by an age before his time. Stainless steel mechanical keyboards rusting silently away in the shadows, towered over by large vertical monitors over a century old. The old laboratory invoked Nostalgia of his grandfather\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s lab tucked away on their farm lab before artificial vertical farming took over. Yet seamlessly preserved. A flickering light whispered across the room as robotic arms loomed seeming to track John\u8217\'92s movement across the shadows. John could feel the lab watching him, luring him towards a dimly lit corner of the lab, an ethereal luminescence pulsates, the chirping static of a struggling light bulb, pulling John in step by step, a colossal steel capsule nestled by the shadows, it\u8217\'92s secrets veiled in the flickering dance of light and darkness.  }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The capsule extruded from the ground all the way to an elevated ceiling which cratered upwards into an amalgamation of pipes and wires feeding from the walls into the foreboding mass of the capsule. The base however presented a humble opening, only human size yet not to the scale of it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s towering height and girth. As John approached closer the seams around the tiny door let out a sharp hiss, spewing steam and dust into the air in a sequence from top to bottom. The door retracted inwards then grinded softly, slowly to the side, inviting the John into its embrace. John found himself lured to this device. As he ran his hand across the door, A military stencil ran in his hands wake, \u8220\'93Cross Integration Chamber\u8221\'94. The room seemed to hum, whispering to him. John felt something deep seated inside him take hold of him, like he could no longer control his own body. He could not veer into the chamber and it\u8217\'92s internal workings, what secrets behold beyond it\u8217\'92s door. He checked his teams vitals one last time before actuating the helmet release from his suit. A sharp click and he had disconnected his helmet from the Mark IV. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 The back of the suit splayed outwards, it\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s rear armour like steel feathers formed the figure of wings, dimly lit now dancing before the chamber with the flickering ambience. John\u8217\'92s body suit shimmered his muscles flexed as he pulled himself from the suit, to a crisp kiss as his feet touched the cold steel grates of the laboratory leaving a pool of gelatinous goop from the neural sync pool within his suit. Like a possessed child being called back to the womb, John slowly undressed. The cold of the room sent chills, his hairs standing on end, unfaltering to the cold he stepped along the grate closer to the Pod\u8217\'92s embrace then paused at it\u8217\'92s opening gently laying his hand on it\u8217\'92s shell. He took one deep breath, and it was done. }
\par\plain {\f0\fs24\b0\i0 John stepped inside the chamber. Suddenly the chamber door closed, sealing him in a pool of pitch-black darkness. A hiss splurted out, as a sleeping agent filled the pod enveloping John\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\af0\uc1\u8217\'92s tattered body with dreams of never-ending tunnels reaching out and onwards like mycelium through a vast network extending far beyond the reaches of the stars he knew. Needle like pinches could be felt all over his body, they weren\u8217\'92t painful, but a pleasant feeling after the first few. Then all fell silent, Johns head fell heavy on his shoulders into a deep sleep, he was at peace in a dream that extended time space and the body itself.}
\par\plain \f0\fs24\b0\i0}